      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#1–#2 · CW11 paraphrase with paragraph locators; the quilt's assumption-of correction (human-amplified: yes)",
          "title": "The incarnation–Assumption chiasm",
          "italic": "The chiasm demonstrates the crossed reading: what a pole does and the field it bear produce different valences — and the return must retain the body that bore the relation.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The movement has two directions. In the first, the maternal matrix receives the Logos into bodily life: what is articulated as divine Word comes through a body which bears it. In the return, that maternal body is itself received — the quilt's correction is assumption-of rather than ascent-away-from: return bears what made manifestation possible instead of discarding the vessel. If only a general feminine principle entered the final account, the particular body would disappear where recognition claims completion. The chiasm then names the crossed readings: articulation, differentiation and explication give 1–2–3 a masculine operation; receiving,",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "containing, reflecting and gathering give 4–5–0 a feminine one — while the older symbolic assignment associates matter with the feminine and mind with the masculine. Both relations are held as the object of inquiry, symbolic assignments being developed, not determinations of what men and women are. Jung's attributed sequence runs from Proverbs' wisdom through the Second Eve to the Assumption discussion and continuing incarnation; his critique of exceptional protections (§§626–627) stays inside his own psychological reading; the proposed Sophia–Logos–Śakti three-office distribution is assistant elaboration (human-amplified: no for the fixed allocation).\n\nOccurrences: the receiving and the received body (#1); the crossed masculine/feminine operations (#2); Jung's §§609–628, 746–757 as attributed paraphrase (#1); the perfection/completeness difficulty (#1).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
